{
  "title": "How many people have been to the Moon?",
  "titleZh": "有多少人去过月球？",
  "source": "Encyclopaedia Britannica / NASA",
  "sourceUrl": "https://www.britannica.com/story/how-many-people-have-been-to-the-moon",
  "lexile": 450,
  "story": {
    "pages": [
      {
        "id": "p1",
        "imageKey": "01",
        "focusWords": [
          "people",
          "Moon",
          "walk",
          "twelve",
          "twenty-four"
        ],
        "en": "How many people have been to the Moon? Twenty-four people went there in the Apollo years. Twelve of them walked on the Moon.",
        "zh": "有多少人去过月球？在阿波罗年代，有24个人去过那里。其中12个人在月球上走过。"
      },
      {
        "id": "p2",
        "imageKey": "02",
        "focusWords": [
          "Apollo",
          "fly",
          "Earth",
          "orbit"
        ],
        "en": "Apollo 8 went first. The crew flew around the Moon. They saw Earth rise over the cold, dark Moon.",
        "zh": "阿波罗8号最先出发。机组绕着月球飞。他们看见地球从又冷又黑的月球上升起。"
      },
      {
        "id": "p3",
        "imageKey": "03",
        "focusWords": [
          "Neil Armstrong",
          "Buzz Aldrin",
          "first",
          "step"
        ],
        "en": "Apollo 11 made a big step. Neil Armstrong was first to walk on the Moon. Buzz Aldrin walked next.",
        "zh": "阿波罗11号迈出了重要一步。尼尔·阿姆斯特朗第一个在月球上行走。巴兹·奥尔德林接着走上去。"
      },
      {
        "id": "p4",
        "imageKey": "04",
        "focusWords": [
          "Michael Collins",
          "ship",
          "orbit",
          "crew"
        ],
        "en": "Michael Collins stayed in the ship. He flew in orbit while his friends walked. He was part of the crew too.",
        "zh": "迈克尔·柯林斯留在飞船上。朋友们在下面走时，他在轨道上飞行。他也是机组的一员。"
      },
      {
        "id": "p5",
        "imageKey": "05",
        "focusWords": [
          "mission",
          "astronaut",
          "footprint",
          "flag"
        ],
        "en": "Later Apollo missions took more astronauts. Twelve people left footprints on the Moon. They put up a flag and looked at rocks.",
        "zh": "后来的阿波罗任务带走了更多宇航员。12个人在月球留下脚印。他们插上旗帜，还观察岩石。"
      },
      {
        "id": "p6",
        "imageKey": "06",
        "focusWords": [
          "far",
          "cold",
          "dark",
          "rocket",
          "ship"
        ],
        "en": "The Moon is far from Earth. It can be cold and dark. Astronauts needed a strong rocket and a special ship.",
        "zh": "月球离地球很远。那里可能又冷又黑。宇航员需要强大的火箭和特别的飞船。"
      },
      {
        "id": "p7",
        "imageKey": "07",
        "focusWords": [
          "NASA",
          "travel",
          "again",
          "return"
        ],
        "en": "After 1972, people stopped walking on the Moon for a long time. But NASA plans new trips. People will travel there again.",
        "zh": "1972年以后，人们很久没有再走上月球。但NASA在计划新的旅行。人们还会再去。"
      },
      {
        "id": "p8",
        "imageKey": "08",
        "focusWords": [
          "twenty-four",
          "twelve",
          "giant",
          "leap"
        ],
        "en": "So how many people have been to the Moon? Start with twenty-four Apollo astronauts. Twelve walked. It was one giant leap for us all.",
        "zh": "那么有多少人去过月球？先从24名阿波罗宇航员算起。12人走过。这对我们所有人是一次巨大飞跃。"
      }
    ]
  },
